answers.body:
Too many "// some code" to be sure, but to me the issue is that you're not releasing the same locks you set, i.e. the value of subarr[k] changes after you call omp_set_lock and before omp_unset_lock . One possible solution would be to make a thread-private variable, e.g. int n = subarr[k];
omp_set_lock(&lock[n]);
// do stuff
omp_unset_lock(&(lock[n])); This ensures that the thread is releasing the same lock it set. As a bonus: you can safely put #pragma omp parallel for on your lock init loop for improved performance.

