Your mandel function has a vastly differing runtime cost depending on whether the if condition within the loop has been met. As a result, each iteration of your loop will run in a different time. By default omp uses static scheduling (i.e. break loop into N partitions) . This is kinda bad, because you don't have a workload that fits static scheduling. See what happens when you use dynamic scheduling. #pragma omp parallel for schedule(dynamic, 1)
for (int y = 0; y < HEIGHT; y++)
    {
       for (int x = 0; x < WIDTH; x++)
