answers.body:
It's actually simple - just make the outer j -loop non-worksharing: #pragma omp parallel
for (int j = 0; j < 2; j++) {
    #pragma omp for schedule(static)
    for (int i = 0; i < 10; i++) {
         ...
    }
} If you use the static schedule, OpenMP guarantees, that each worker will get to handle the same range of i s for both j=0 and j=1 . Note: You moving the parallel construct to the outer loop is merely an optimization to avoid thread management overhead. The code works similarly if you just place a parallel for in-between the two loops.

